  "about": "Twenty-four of the most common words in children's books, from the Dolch and Fry high-frequency lists, that are not on his CKLA tricky-word lists and not in another level (and, had, will, came, just). Most can be sounded out with code he knows and only a few have a pink part; the goal is to know them at a glance, which is what NC RF.1.4.g and smooth reading are built on.",
  "tip": "Flash each card for two seconds: he should say it straight away, and only sound it out if he gets stuck.",
  "cards": [
